00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:37.960
I've never seen you miss before.

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.300
I've also never seen you shrink away from responsibility,

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.340
no matter how difficult.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:46.900
You saw the look on those guys' faces.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:47.780
I couldn't let them down.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.840
Just thought I could find a way to play like everyone else.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:55.160
Clark.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.340
Open your hand.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.120
What are you doing?

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.000
You know how dangerous kryptonite is.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.860
Well, I always get better after it's gone.

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.080
So what if I'm playing sick? Other guys play injured.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:15.200
And if Dad knows I don't have my abilities and I can't hurt anyone...

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.960
You are not taking meteor rocks out on that field.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.220
I know this is hard. You can't make yourself sick.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:21.500
And I can't quit either.

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.100
Clark, the answer is no.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:26.420
You asked your father to help you.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.019
I would have asked my father if we'd ever seen you trip before.

00:16:28.259 --> 00:16:28.539
Never.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.559
Not without kryptonite.

00:16:35.099 --> 00:16:38.579
I was so excited to see you get a chance to be like everyone else

00:16:38.579 --> 00:16:41.839
that I guess I forgot for a moment that you aren't.

00:16:42.819 --> 00:16:44.959
I didn't think anything of it when you tripped,

00:16:45.079 --> 00:16:48.979
but you've never had mishaps like other kids.

00:16:52.059 --> 00:16:53.980
Something happened to you out there.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:54.019
I don't know.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:55.480
I don't know.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.179
And if you really want to...

00:16:56.419 --> 00:16:57.559
play in the game on Saturday,

00:16:58.299 --> 00:16:59.919
you need to find out what it was.

00:17:12.799 --> 00:17:14.200
It's all right, Clark. You can stay.

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:18.879
I thought you had some self-imposed restraining order against me.

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:20.039
Does this mean you're talking to me again?

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.440
No, this just means that I'm willing to take a chance

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.980
on getting your Dr. Jekyll side today.

00:17:25.159 --> 00:17:26.139
What's up with this?

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.000
Self-flogging.

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.380
I'm watching the sports editor's tape of the game,

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:32.020
trying to figure out what happened, but...

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:35.000
It's like I had no control.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.300
Like my mind was sending one message, but...

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.720
But your body was getting another.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:39.880
Yeah.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:41.380
It's Mikhail.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.720
The foreign exchange kid?

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:45.259
Mixa...

00:17:45.259 --> 00:17:46.540
Mixalpitalik.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.320
Say that three times fast.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:50.220
He's our new resident puppet master.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:55.940
This is kind of embarrassing, but he made me kiss him.

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:58.520
He made you?

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:04.280
Yeah, it was just like how you explained your trip.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.680
It was like someone else was controlling me.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.940
Okay, but why would he want me to throw the game?

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.740
Clark, he's the biggest bookie in the school.

00:18:14.259 --> 00:18:15.920
The power to control the odds.

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.120
Let me do a search on his name.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.780
I guess I shouldn't be surprised that Mixalpitalik didn't bring anything up.

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.500
Well, what's that?

00:18:31.759 --> 00:18:33.660
It's Mikhail's name backwards.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.040
Looks like a nursery rhyme gone bad.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:44.100
Yeah, it's some legend from the Piatore region in the Balkans.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.500
That's near where Mikhail's from.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.860
It says the region has been terrorized for centuries by a bloodline of people

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.120
who have been...

00:18:56.119 --> 00:18:57.879
Who can control the hand of luck.

00:18:58.859 --> 00:19:00.899
It's not exactly luck if they're controlling people.

00:19:01.099 --> 00:19:03.099
What does it say about the backwards name?

00:19:04.179 --> 00:19:06.179
The family changed their name a century ago

00:19:06.179 --> 00:19:07.699
and fled the area to escape the stigma

00:19:07.699 --> 00:19:09.539
after a village mysteriously burned to the ground.

00:19:10.239 --> 00:19:12.299
Looks like Mikhail's still running from his heritage.

00:19:12.719 --> 00:19:16.179
It doesn't exactly say how to stop the kissing bandit, does it?

00:19:16.799 --> 00:19:17.419
Oh, here.

00:19:17.739 --> 00:19:20.059
According to the legends, the only thing that stopped them

00:19:20.059 --> 00:19:21.939
was a plague of locusts.

00:19:22.339 --> 00:19:24.199
There may be one other force they didn't count on.

00:19:26.119 --> 00:19:28.439
Think about it.

00:19:28.439 --> 00:19:29.799
Who brought him here in the first place?

00:19:32.799 --> 00:19:35.619
You want me to deport a Luther Corp exchange student?

00:19:37.639 --> 00:19:41.179
Gambling on Crows games isn't a sanctioned extracurricular.

00:19:41.899 --> 00:19:44.619
I'm surprised you care so much about some half-rate bookie.

00:19:45.339 --> 00:19:47.479
Or is there something else about Mikhail you're not telling me?

00:19:48.679 --> 00:19:49.779
Lex, you sponsored him.

00:19:49.819 --> 00:19:51.599
I just thought you might want to do something about it.

00:19:52.719 --> 00:19:54.219
Of course I'll look into it.

00:19:55.259 --> 00:19:55.899
Though I'm surprised you're not.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:58.440
I'm surprised you didn't go to the principal first, or Coach Teague.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:02.019
But then I could see how that could be more complicated than it sounds.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.980
Why would it be more complicated?

00:20:09.019 --> 00:20:09.640
Come on.

00:20:10.519 --> 00:20:13.600
I can't be the only one who's picked up on my mom's fondness for quarterbacks.

00:20:14.259 --> 00:20:15.580
Even retired ones.

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:21.360
Yeah, to be honest, it has been hard to see her with someone else.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:24.000
Don't worry.

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:26.960
Paris can have a magical effect on people,

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:30.839
but the enchantment has a funny way of waning the longer you're gone.

00:20:31.779 --> 00:20:32.660
I know Lana.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.799
She's never been this serious about anyone.

00:20:36.539 --> 00:20:40.059
You sound awfully concerned about that for someone who let her walk out of his life.

00:20:43.099 --> 00:20:46.279
Yeah, I guess the whole if you love them, set them free thing kind of backfired.

00:20:46.519 --> 00:20:47.759
It's not about love, Clark.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:50.420
It's about what you're willing to do for it.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:53.980
On that field, you'll do whatever it takes to win.

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.500
But if you're not willing to do the same for Lana,

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.759
maybe she doesn't mean as much to you as you think.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:10.539
Clark on steroids.

00:21:11.039 --> 00:21:12.240
It's a little hard to picture.

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.619
It happens to a lot of guys.

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.079
They want so badly to outperform everyone,

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:20.240
before you know it, all they care about is winning, no matter what the cost.

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:22.940
You're not responsible for that.

00:21:23.059 --> 00:21:23.700
I am.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.500
You're not responsible for Clark.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:27.500
Actually, I am.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:30.500
Coach Kugli asked me to give him a drug test,

00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:32.000
and I never mentioned it to Clark,

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.000
so I lied and said it came back clean.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.000
Why would you do that?

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.000
I don't know.

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.500
Because I believe in Clark,

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.000
and because he knows about us.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.000
I didn't want to stir the waters.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.000
If he wanted to get back at me,

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.000
all he's got to do is tell somebody at the school,

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:47.000
and I lose my job.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:48.000
Clark wouldn't make it personal.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.000
Why not?

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:53.000
I mean, I can't imagine what I would do if someone tried to take you away from me.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.000
Nobody took me away from Clark.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.000
I left.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Right.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:03.000
Clark's a big part of the reason why I took off for Paris in the first place.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:08.000
Oh, that must be from the book of things you never want to hear about your girlfriend's ex.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:12.000
Look, Jason, I'm with you now, and I couldn't be happier.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.000
And I know, I know, Clark can be unpredictable,

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.000
but he knows that you need this job to stay in college.

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:24.000
I know it's hard because you've been so close to him,

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:26.000
but are you sure you really know him?

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.000
Don't get me wrong, Mikhail,

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:41.000
I appreciate your entrepreneurial ingenuity,

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.000
but importing bookies tends to reflect poorly on a company.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.000
These are just fun games.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.000
The INS isn't exactly where you want to be.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:50.000
They're renowned for their good sportsmanship.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.000
They're revoking your student visa and sending you back home.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:55.000
But a man like you can pull strings to keep me here, yes?

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:58.000
If I wanted to.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:01.000
But whatever talents my father saw in you,

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:04.000
they're not worth the embarrassment you bring to me and my company.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:08.000
I've made the arrangements.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:10.000
You'll be halfway over the Atlantic by morning.

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:12.000
You don't really want that.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:16.000
You want to know why your dad brought me here.

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:18.000
Not that badly.

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:20.000
What if we make a wager?

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:23.000
Now, why would I take a bet when I could just have you thrown out of here?

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.000
Because I know gamblers better than anybody.

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:28.000
You're the caviar kind.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.000
See, when you hold everything in your hand,

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.000
the only thing that can give you a thrill

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:36.000
is putting your chips on the one thing that can slip through your fingers.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:45.000
And, uh, what would that one thing that you're holding in your hand mean?

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.000
What would that one thing mean, McCown?

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:49.000
Well, in this case, me.

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:56.000
How much do you believe in this quarterback friend of yours, Clark Kent?

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.000
The championship game?

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.000
What's the wager?

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:08.000
If the Crows lose, you'll reign citizenship for me

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.000
and $1 million to start a new game.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:12.000
And if the Crows win,

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:15.000
I have a hard time believing you can cover

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:17.000
that bet.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:18.000
I can't.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:20.000
But the reason your father brought me here

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:22.000
is far more valuable than just money.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:36.000
Oh, look.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:40.000
A real-life American football superhero.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
What are you doing here?

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:44.000
I came here to thank you for...

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:47.000
renting me out to Lex.

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:49.000
It wasn't hard to figure out.

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:52.000
I knew Chloe would squeal, just not to him.

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:54.000
She's too proud.

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:58.000
You seem to be the common denominator, so...

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:01.000
you forget games are my business,

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:03.000
so if you don't know the players,

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:05.000
you cannot guess the outcome.

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:10.000
I thought you'd be halfway back to the Village of the Damned by now.

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:12.000
I'm not cursed, Clark.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:13.000
I am lucky.

00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:16.000
And on Saturday in the championship game,

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:18.000
I'm going to be very lucky.

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:20.000
You think I'm gonna throw that game for you?

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.000
If...

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:24.000
When there is an if, there are odds.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.000
And I always beat the odds.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:28.000
Joke.

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:32.000
For example,

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:35.000
the odds in the championship are based on your playing.

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:37.000
If you don't go out in the field,

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:40.000
then my profit margin takes an unfortunate turn.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.000
That is why you're not going to win.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:45.000
That is why you're not going to tell anyone else about me.

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:48.000
And you are going to be on that field.

00:25:48.000 --> 00:25:49.000
Unless...

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:53.000
you want to see more of your buddies in the hospital.

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:02.000
Breathe.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:16.000
SCHOOL B lowers

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:19.000
Chloe.

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:20.000
Hey.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.000
Clark.

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:22.000
Break up in 15 minutes.

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:25.000
I sure hope you have had better luck with the locusts

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:26.000
than I did with Lex.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:27.000
The last time I came back,

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.000
they weren't selling biblical seals on Amazon.

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:31.000
But now that a legend is born in the seed of truth,

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:33.000
we'll take up our favorite critters again.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.000
Besides eating weeds in a single webinar,

00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:37.000
What else can they do?

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:38.000
When locust swarms,

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:40.000
they emit an enery wave to preventchw poder crash into them.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.000
Maybe Mikhail Kumano outfied him,

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:44.460
Maybe Mikhail's commands operate on a similar frequency, you know, like a radio signal.

00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:47.380
Or a dog whistle. The sound travels, but the human ear doesn't pick it up.

00:26:47.579 --> 00:26:51.039
Yeah. Now, what's interesting is that once Locus's signals are jammed,

00:26:51.200 --> 00:26:54.140
they can't fly anymore without running into each other. It's permanent.

00:26:54.980 --> 00:26:58.160
Well, maybe all we have to do is find something that will jam Mikhail's frequency for good.

00:26:58.720 --> 00:27:01.819
And I think I know just where to find that, so now we just have to find him.

00:27:02.099 --> 00:27:05.539
Oh, in his quest for the great American dream, he's got a lot of bets riding on this game.

00:27:05.599 --> 00:27:06.099
He'll be here.

00:27:07.019 --> 00:27:07.380
Okay.

00:27:07.779 --> 00:27:08.279
I gotta go.

00:27:08.359 --> 00:27:08.700
Good luck.

00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:09.339
Thanks.

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:17.380
Greetings, football fans, and welcome to the championship game

00:27:17.380 --> 00:27:21.779
between the Topeka Valley Huskies and your small Bill Crows.

00:27:21.819 --> 00:27:27.500
I walk a lonely road, the only one that I have ever known.

00:27:27.759 --> 00:27:33.400
Don't know where it goes, but it's only me and I walk alone.

00:27:38.400 --> 00:27:40.980
I walk this empty street.

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:44.779
On the boulevard of broken dreams.

00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:50.599
Where the city sleeps and I'm the only one and I walk alone.

00:27:52.680 --> 00:27:56.400
I walk alone, I walk alone.

00:27:58.420 --> 00:28:01.680
I walk alone, I walk alone.

00:28:02.220 --> 00:28:07.420
My shadow's all in one that walks beside me.

00:28:07.420 --> 00:28:10.559
My shadow heart.

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.000
My lonely fan that's fading.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.000
Sunshine.

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.000
All right, let's go.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:16.000
All right.

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:17.000
Let's go.

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:18.000
Let's go.

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:19.000
Come on.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.000
Come on.

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:21.000
Keep it all out in the field.

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:22.000
You have to.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:23.000
